{"title":"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What are the last two digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c002566606b9154bc641f7538defc73bdb8f91d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2017^{2017}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In this problem, we will use the Chinese remainder theorem. This question is asking us to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9ffc7d255cf4e17a9c4f5d4e760e497e28939d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2017^{2017}\\mod 100=17^{2017}\\mod 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"293\" height=\"15\" />. By the Chinese remainder theorem, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80c7228941fc7416a74cdf1df0822f72faf91c55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17^{2017}\\mod 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a8f1387f274a651df03dce48de9a419c48c1e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17^{2017}\\mod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, and then \"combine\" them. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d140f96116911500b9d7c6dd2841f0e3482b3269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17^{2017}\\mod4\\equiv1^{2017}\\mod4\\equiv1\\mod4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"325\" height=\"15\" />. To find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63ee15589d2612ff92921a9657cd2aaac5bcab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17^{2017}\\mod25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" />, we'll look for a pattern. The pattern is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/9992fd80bcf9c25291c7c7969c3acaff343903c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17, 14, 13, 21, 7, 19, 23, 16, 22, -1, -17, -14, -13, -21, -7, -19, -23, -16, -22, 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"621\" height=\"16\" />. Since there are 20 terms, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa50496da9b1d1408e87020311af95899b55bb8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2017\\equiv17\\mod20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"152\" height=\"14\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c799e7a5c63359d69b2f779a1c1b661070c45f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17^{2017}\\mod25\\equiv2\\mod25$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"220\" height=\"15\" />. Now, we want to find a number that's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fda075bd8294bd47eda423f4bc1a01d096c4fd79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\mod25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b83cd63440a70114e304e4bba758160cfd9964.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\mod4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />. We find this number by clever guess and check. We know our number is odd, so it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f28a9804949690f057cbca3943d25f93f03ebee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27\\mod50$\" width=\"88\" height=\"12\" />. First, we try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, but that doesn't work. Next, we try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af4b3f8897671e2879b10badf471e5deec8952e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$77$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />, and that works! So, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/54994fa6a40d5dca1c24208f8b55c441fcc0e532.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{77}\\]\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />\n<i>-bronzetruck2016<i>\n</i></i></p><i><i><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2></i></i><i><i><table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II\">2017 UNM-PNM Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://mathcontest.unm.edu/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a hre